<title>USA: Hanover completes $50m shr rights offering.</title>
<headline>Hanover completes $50m shr rights offering.</headline>
<dateline>WEEHAWKEN, N.J. 1997-06-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Hanover Direct Inc said it completed a $50 million shareholder rights offering.</p>
<p>The company will use the offering's proceeds to repay $30 million advanced to the company in April by Richemont Finance of the Swiss tabacco and luxury goods group Compagnie Financiere Richemont AG, a company statement said. It will further use the funds to strengthen its balance sheet and improve its liquidity, it added.</p>
<p>&quot;The company's revolving debt has been completely repaid and the company is in a net cash investment position of approximately $5 million, said chief executive Rakesh Kaul.</p>
